Real Spectre PSF ASCII output files (docs/VAMOS_SPECTRE_DESIGN.md: the [S] row of §0, §8, §11
"psfcheck").  Every file below was written by Cadence Spectre and is copied byte for byte from a
public repository, so that psfcheck.py (tests/vamos) is held to what Spectre writes: it must accept
every one of them (test_spectre_psfcheck.TestRealSamples).  Licences, repository URLs and commits
are in ../../README; the summary is in the repository's LICENSE.

One line per file: path, the Spectre version from its "version" header, its "analysis type" (a
logFile has none), and its "date" header.

psf-parser (MIT), repository ToonBettens/psf-parser on GitHub, commit
05021e6e62cdb9aebf1ee1a98609bb4b3a4f2d16: tests/data/ascii is one Spectre 23.1.0.242.isr1 run of the
design "#RC Low-Pass Filter" (an op, a dc sweep, an ac, a tran, three info files, a sweep with a nested
sweep, and a three-iteration Monte Carlo); tests/data/binary/logFile is that run's logFile, written in
ASCII although the data files of that directory are psfbin (the ASCII data files above are the same
analyses written as psfascii, so the logFile's 38 dataFile entries name exactly them; check it with
"psfcheck.py --datadir psf-parser/tests/data/ascii psf-parser/tests/data/binary/logFile").

